% Portable regex: the parts of SPEC 7.8 that are already decided, held to every host.
%
% Family T06 of the 2026-09-29 review remediation. Every case's expectation is
% derived from spec/SPEC.md 7.8, spec/errors.md and spec/limits.json, never from a
% host's output. Patterns are raw '...' literals because `{` in "..." is
% interpolation. Catastrophic backtracking is pinned separately, in
% conformance/28b-regex-ambiguity.selt; tools/check-regex-resources.py runs the
% bounded child-process probes (a suite must not hang).

### name: re.reject.quantified-anchor.1
--- note
SPEC 7.8: the subset is the intersection of what every engine accepts. ECMAScript-with-u, PCRE and Python reject a quantifier applied to an anchor; cl-ppcre and RE2-style engines accepted it, so the subset checker has to reject it itself rather than delegate (LISP-C11, GO-C28, JS-C45, CPP-C49).
--- source
RMATCH('^*', "aaa")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

