### name: re.reject.class-escape-range-endpoint.1
--- note
A class escape cannot be a range endpoint: ECMAScript-with-u rejects it and PCRE reads the hyphen literally, so the two disagree and the intersection is a rejection. Rewriting `\d` to `0-9` in place used to turn the neighbouring hyphen into an accidental range (`[+-\d]` matched `,` and not `5`) (PHP-C18, JS-C43, CPP-C49, GO-C31).
--- source
RMATCH('[+-\d]', "5")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.class-escape-range-endpoint.2
--- note
A class escape cannot be a range endpoint: ECMAScript-with-u rejects it and PCRE reads the hyphen literally, so the two disagree and the intersection is a rejection. Rewriting `\d` to `0-9` in place used to turn the neighbouring hyphen into an accidental range (`[+-\d]` matched `,` and not `5`) (PHP-C18, JS-C43, CPP-C49, GO-C31).
--- source
RMATCH('[\d-z]', "5")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.class-escape-range-endpoint.3
