### name: re.accept.class-escape-with-literal-hyphen-at-the-edge
--- note
CONTROL for the group above: a hyphen that is first or last in the class is a literal in every engine, next to an escape or not.
--- source
RMATCH('^[\d-]$', "-") AND RMATCH('^[-\d]$', "-") AND RMATCH('^[\w.-]$', "-") AND RMATCH('^[\d-]$', "7")
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.accept.class-escape-plus-punctuation
--- note
CONTROL: an escape followed by ordinary members is expanded in place.
--- source
RMATCH('^[\d.]$', ".") AND NOT RMATCH('^[\d.]$', "x")
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.reject.posix-class-anywhere.1
--- note
SPEC 7.8 rejects POSIX classes, and a `[:name:]` is one wherever it stands in the class. PHP raised for `[a[:digit:]` while four hosts matched it as a literal class (JS-C18, PHP-C19).
--- source
RMATCH('[a[:alpha:]]', "a")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.posix-class-anywhere.2
--- note
SPEC 7.8 rejects POSIX classes, and a `[:name:]` is one wherever it stands in the class. PHP raised for `[a[:digit:]` while four hosts matched it as a literal class (JS-C18, PHP-C19).
--- source
RMATCH('[a[:digit:]', "a")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.posix-class-anywhere.3
--- note
SPEC 7.8 rejects POSIX classes, and a `[:name:]` is one wherever it stands in the class. PHP raised for `[a[:digit:]` while four hosts matched it as a literal class (JS-C18, PHP-C19).
--- source
RMATCH('[x[:^alpha:]]', "a")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.posix-class-anywhere.4
--- note
SPEC 7.8 rejects POSIX classes, and a `[:name:]` is one wherever it stands in the class. PHP raised for `[a[:digit:]` while four hosts matched it as a literal class (JS-C18, PHP-C19).
--- source
RMATCH('[[:alpha:]a]', "a")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.pcre-verb.1
--- note
`(*` is not in the subset: ECMAScript reads it as a quantifier with nothing to repeat. PCRE verbs changed what PHP matched (`a(*ACCEPT)b` matched `ac`) (PHP-C4, CPP-C49).
--- source
RMATCH('(*FAIL)', "ac")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.pcre-verb.2
--- note
`(*` is not in the subset: ECMAScript reads it as a quantifier with nothing to repeat. PCRE verbs changed what PHP matched (`a(*ACCEPT)b` matched `ac`) (PHP-C4, CPP-C49).
--- source
RMATCH('a(*ACCEPT)b', "ac")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.pcre-verb.3
--- note
`(*` is not in the subset: ECMAScript reads it as a quantifier with nothing to repeat. PCRE verbs changed what PHP matched (`a(*ACCEPT)b` matched `ac`) (PHP-C4, CPP-C49).
--- source
RMATCH('(*UTF8)a', "ac")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.pcre-verb.4
--- note
`(*` is not in the subset: ECMAScript reads it as a quantifier with nothing to repeat. PCRE verbs changed what PHP matched (`a(*ACCEPT)b` matched `ac`) (PHP-C4, CPP-C49).
--- source
RMATCH('(*COMMIT)a', "ac")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.pcre-verb.5
--- note
`(*` is not in the subset: ECMAScript reads it as a quantifier with nothing to repeat. PCRE verbs changed what PHP matched (`a(*ACCEPT)b` matched `ac`) (PHP-C4, CPP-C49).
--- source
RMATCH('(*ANY)a', "ac")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.pcre-verb.6
--- note
`(*` is not in the subset: ECMAScript reads it as a quantifier with nothing to repeat. PCRE verbs changed what PHP matched (`a(*ACCEPT)b` matched `ac`) (PHP-C4, CPP-C49).
--- source
RMATCH('(*LIMIT_MATCH=1)a', "ac")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.flag.uppercase-i-is-not-i
--- note
SPEC 7.8: 'Flags: `i` and nothing else.' Uppercase `I` was accepted everywhere through each host's own case folding (JS-C44, LISP-C37).
--- source
RMATCH('a', "A", "I")
--- expect
error E_BAD_ARG
===

### name: re.flag.dotted-capital-i-is-not-a-flag
--- note
U+0130 lower-cases to `i` under some case mappings; the flag test is ASCII-only (LISP-C37).
--- source
RMATCH('a', "A", "\u{130}")
--- expect
error E_BAD_ARG
===

### name: re.flag.dotless-i-is-not-a-flag
--- note
U+0131 upper-cases to `I`; same rule.
--- source
RMATCH('a', "A", "\u{131}")
--- expect
error E_BAD_ARG
===

### name: re.flag.kelvin-sign-is-not-a-flag
--- note
U+212A lower-cases to `k`, not `i`, but no non-ASCII character is a flag.
--- source
RMATCH('a', "a", "\u{212A}")
--- expect
error E_BAD_ARG
===

### name: re.flag.lowercase-i-still-works
--- note
CONTROL.
--- source
RMATCH('^a+$', "AaA", "i")
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.repeat.1001-matches
--- note
Counted repeats above 1000 silently became `never matches` in Go (RE2's own cap); the subset says the cap is 65535 (GO-C1).
--- source
RMATCH('^a{1001}$', REPEAT("a", 1001))
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.repeat.1000-times-2-matches
--- note
GO-C1: a product of counted repeats, each below the cap.
--- source
RMATCH('^(?:a{1000}){2}$', REPEAT("a", 2000))
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.repeat.open-ended-1001
--- note
GO-C1: `{n,}` above 1000.
--- source
RMATCH('^a{1001,}$', REPEAT("a", 1001))
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.repeat.upper-bound-2000-matches-empty
--- note
GO-C1.
--- source
RMATCH('^a{0,2000}$', "")
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.repeat.upper-bound-5000-finds
--- note
GO-C1: RFIND through the same bound.
--- source
RFIND('b{2,5000}', "abb")
--- expect
num 2
===

### name: re.repeat.leading-zeros
--- note
`{00001}` is `{1}` in every engine that accepts it; Go turned it into `never matches` (GO-C1).
--- source
RMATCH('^a{00001}$', "a")
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.repeat.300-times-300
--- note
GO-C1: 90,000 characters through nested counted repeats.
--- source
RMATCH('^(a{300}){300}$', REPEAT("a", 90000))
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.repeat.at-the-cap-with-a-matching-subject
--- note
re.quantifier.bound-at-the-cap only proves FALSE; a matching subject is what shows the cap is honoured rather than silently turned into `never matches`.
--- source
RMATCH('^a{65535}$', REPEAT("a", 65535))
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.repeat.at-the-cap-one-short-of-a-match
--- note
The same pattern on one character less is FALSE, not an error.
--- source
RMATCH('^a{65535}$', REPEAT("a", 65534))
--- expect
bool FALSE
===

### name: re.repeat.beyond-the-cap-lower-bound
--- note
The cap applies to either bound of a range.
--- source
RMATCH('a{65536,}', "a")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.repeat.beyond-the-cap-upper-bound
--- note

--- source
RMATCH('a{1,65536}', "a")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.literal.checked-at-compile-time.1
--- note
SPEC 7.8 and errors.md: a literal pattern is checked at compile time, so a bad one is `E_REGEX_SYNTAX` even in a branch that never runs. Every host used to validate lazily, at the call (PY-C35, CPP-C28).
--- source
IF(FALSE, RMATCH('(?=a)', "a"), 1)
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.literal.checked-at-compile-time.2
--- note
SPEC 7.8 and errors.md: a literal pattern is checked at compile time, so a bad one is `E_REGEX_SYNTAX` even in a branch that never runs. Every host used to validate lazily, at the call (PY-C35, CPP-C28).
--- source
IF(FALSE, RFIND('(?=a)', "a"), 1)
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.literal.checked-at-compile-time.3
--- note
SPEC 7.8 and errors.md: a literal pattern is checked at compile time, so a bad one is `E_REGEX_SYNTAX` even in a branch that never runs. Every host used to validate lazily, at the call (PY-C35, CPP-C28).
--- source
IF(FALSE, RREPLACE('(?=a)', "-", "a"), 1)
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.literal.checked-at-compile-time.4
--- note
SPEC 7.8 and errors.md: a literal pattern is checked at compile time, so a bad one is `E_REGEX_SYNTAX` even in a branch that never runs. Every host used to validate lazily, at the call (PY-C35, CPP-C28).
--- source
IF(FALSE, RGROUPS('(?=a)', "a"), 1)
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.literal.checked-at-compile-time.5
--- note
SPEC 7.8 and errors.md: a literal pattern is checked at compile time, so a bad one is `E_REGEX_SYNTAX` even in a branch that never runs. Every host used to validate lazily, at the call (PY-C35, CPP-C28).
--- source
IF(FALSE, RMATCH("(?=a)", "a"), 1)
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.computed-pattern.checked-only-when-executed
--- note
errors.md: a pattern built at run time is validated when the call executes, so the same bad pattern in a dead branch is fine.
--- source
IF(FALSE, RMATCH("(?=" & "a)", "a"), 1)
--- expect
num 1
===

### name: re.computed-pattern.checked-when-executed
--- note
... and an error when it does run.
--- source
IF(TRUE, RMATCH("(?=" & "a)", "a"), 1)
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.anchor.end-then-dotstar.match
--- note
`$` matches at the end of the subject and `.*` then matches the empty rest; cl-ppcre never matched `\z.*` (LISP-C10).
--- source
RMATCH('$.*', "abc")
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.anchor.end-then-dotstar.find
--- note

--- source
RFIND('$.*', "abc")
--- expect
num 4
===

### name: re.anchor.end-then-dotstar.replace
--- note

--- source
RREPLACE('$.*', "!", "abc")
--- expect
text "abc!"
===

### name: re.class.open-bracket-member
--- note
`[[]` is a valid class with `[` in it; Python's re warned (FutureWarning, an exception under -W error) (PY-C33).
--- source
RMATCH('^[[]$', "[")
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.class.ampersands-are-literal
--- note
`&&` is a literal pair in every subset engine; Python warned about set operations (PY-C33).
--- source
RMATCH('^[a&&b]$', "&")
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.class.bars-are-literal
--- note

--- source
RMATCH('^[a||b]$', "|")
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.class.tildes-are-literal
--- note

--- source
RMATCH('^[a~~b]$', "~")
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.class.double-hyphen-is-a-reversed-range
--- note
`a--b` is the range a..`-`, out of order, in every engine.
--- source
RMATCH('[a--b]', "a")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.replace.empty-match-abutting-a-match
--- note
A zero-width match at the position where the previous match ended IS a match (ECMAScript, PCRE and Python agree): `a*` on `baac` matches empty at 0, `aa` at 1, empty at 3, empty at 4. Go's regexp dropped the abutting one (GO-C10).
--- source
RREPLACE('a*', "-", "baac")
--- expect
text "-b--c-"
===

### name: re.replace.empty-match-abutting-a-match-space
--- note
GO-C10.
--- source
RREPLACE('\s*', "_", "a b")
--- expect
text "_a__b_"
===

### name: re.replace.empty-match-abutting-with-capture
--- note
GO-C10, with a group and a non-ASCII class.
--- source
RREPLACE('(b*|[é-ü])', "<$0|$1>", "baac")
--- expect
text "<b|b><|>a<|>a<|>c<|>"
===

### name: re.long-subject.match
--- note
PCRE's backtrack/JIT limits turned `^(?:a|b)*$` on 60,000 characters into FALSE in PHP while the other hosts said TRUE: a resource failure must never masquerade as a result (PHP-C3).
--- source
RMATCH('^(?:a|b)*$', REPEAT("a", 60000))
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.long-subject.find
--- note
PHP-C3.
--- source
RFIND('(?:a|b)*c', REPEAT("a", 60000) & "c")
--- expect
num 1
===

### name: re.long-subject.replace
--- note
PHP-C3: the text came back unchanged.
--- source
LEN(RREPLACE('^(?:a|b)*$', "X", REPEAT("a", 60000)))
--- expect
num 1
===

### name: re.long-subject.groups
--- note
PHP-C3.
--- source
COUNT(RGROUPS('^(?:a|b)*$', REPEAT("a", 60000)))
--- expect
num 1
===

### name: re.long-subject.alternation-prefix-of-another
--- note
cl-ppcre exhausted its control stack on `^(?:ab|a)*$` over 30,000 characters (LISP-C3).
--- source
RMATCH('^(?:ab|a)*$', REPEAT("a", 30000))
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.long-subject.captured-alternation
--- note
The same shape with a capture, whose per-iteration bookkeeping is what deepens the recursion.
--- source
RMATCH('^(a|b)*$', REPEAT("ab", 30000))
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.long-subject.counted-capture
--- note
cl-ppcre: `^(a){20000}$` (LISP-C3).
--- source
RMATCH('^(a){20000}$', REPEAT("a", 20000))
--- expect
bool TRUE
===
### name: re.reject.nullable-loop-body.1
--- note
SPEC 7.8: a group whose body can match the empty string may not be quantified. PCRE/Python/cl-ppcre and ECMAScript disagree on both the captures and the overall match of an empty iteration (PY-C4, LISP-C18, CPP-C27, GO-C30); C++ already rejects `(?:^)+`.
--- source
RMATCH('(a*)*', "aab")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===
### name: re.reject.nullable-loop-body.2
--- note
SPEC 7.8: a group whose body can match the empty string may not be quantified. PCRE/Python/cl-ppcre and ECMAScript disagree on both the captures and the overall match of an empty iteration (PY-C4, LISP-C18, CPP-C27, GO-C30); C++ already rejects `(?:^)+`.
--- source
RMATCH('(?:a?)+', "aab")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.nullable-loop-body.3
--- note
SPEC 7.8: a group whose body can match the empty string may not be quantified. PCRE/Python/cl-ppcre and ECMAScript disagree on both the captures and the overall match of an empty iteration (PY-C4, LISP-C18, CPP-C27, GO-C30); C++ already rejects `(?:^)+`.
--- source
RMATCH('(|a)+', "aab")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.nullable-loop-body.4
--- note
SPEC 7.8: a group whose body can match the empty string may not be quantified. PCRE/Python/cl-ppcre and ECMAScript disagree on both the captures and the overall match of an empty iteration (PY-C4, LISP-C18, CPP-C27, GO-C30); C++ already rejects `(?:^)+`.
--- source
RMATCH('(a*?)+', "aab")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.nullable-loop-body.5
--- note
SPEC 7.8: a group whose body can match the empty string may not be quantified. PCRE/Python/cl-ppcre and ECMAScript disagree on both the captures and the overall match of an empty iteration (PY-C4, LISP-C18, CPP-C27, GO-C30); C++ already rejects `(?:^)+`.
--- source
RMATCH('(?:(a)|b?)*', "aab")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.nullable-loop-body.6
--- note
SPEC 7.8: a group whose body can match the empty string may not be quantified. PCRE/Python/cl-ppcre and ECMAScript disagree on both the captures and the overall match of an empty iteration (PY-C4, LISP-C18, CPP-C27, GO-C30); C++ already rejects `(?:^)+`.
--- source
RMATCH('(?:^)*a', "aab")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.nullable-loop-body.7
--- note
SPEC 7.8: a group whose body can match the empty string may not be quantified. PCRE/Python/cl-ppcre and ECMAScript disagree on both the captures and the overall match of an empty iteration (PY-C4, LISP-C18, CPP-C27, GO-C30); C++ already rejects `(?:^)+`.
--- source
RMATCH('(a|)+b', "aab")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.optional-capture-in-loop.1
--- note
SPEC 7.8: inside a quantified group every capture must take part in every iteration; otherwise PCRE keeps the last value and ECMAScript resets it (PHP-C21, PY-C4, CPP-C27, LISP-C18, GO-C30).
--- source
RGROUPS('(?:(a)|b)*', "abab")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.optional-capture-in-loop.2
--- note
SPEC 7.8: inside a quantified group every capture must take part in every iteration; otherwise PCRE keeps the last value and ECMAScript resets it (PHP-C21, PY-C4, CPP-C27, LISP-C18, GO-C30).
--- source
RGROUPS('(?:(a)|(b))+', "abab")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.optional-capture-in-loop.3
--- note
SPEC 7.8: inside a quantified group every capture must take part in every iteration; otherwise PCRE keeps the last value and ECMAScript resets it (PHP-C21, PY-C4, CPP-C27, LISP-C18, GO-C30).
--- source
RGROUPS('((a)|(b))*', "abab")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.optional-capture-in-loop.4
--- note
SPEC 7.8: inside a quantified group every capture must take part in every iteration; otherwise PCRE keeps the last value and ECMAScript resets it (PHP-C21, PY-C4, CPP-C27, LISP-C18, GO-C30).
--- source
RGROUPS('(?:(a)?b)+', "abab")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.optional-capture-in-loop.5
--- note
SPEC 7.8: inside a quantified group every capture must take part in every iteration; otherwise PCRE keeps the last value and ECMAScript resets it (PHP-C21, PY-C4, CPP-C27, LISP-C18, GO-C30).
--- source
RGROUPS('(?:(a)|b){2}', "abab")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.groups.loop-capture-last-iteration
--- note
CONTROL: a capture that always participates keeps its LAST iteration in every engine.
--- source
RGROUPS('(a|b)+', "ab")
--- expect
tree -{"1"=t"ab", "2"=t"b"}
===

### name: re.groups.loop-nested-captures
--- note
CONTROL for P2.
--- source
RGROUPS('((a)b)+', "abab")
--- expect
tree -{"1"=t"abab", "2"=t"ab", "3"=t"a"}
===

### name: re.groups.counted-loop-capture
--- note
CONTROL for P2.
--- source
RGROUPS('(\d)-(\d)', "1-2")
--- expect
tree -{"1"=t"1-2", "2"=t"1", "3"=t"2"}
===

### name: re.replace.lazy-empty-then-nonempty
--- note
SPEC 7.8: after an EMPTY match at s the scan resumes at s+1 (one code point, copied through); after a non-empty match it resumes at its end, where an empty match is allowed. That is what JS, Python and Lisp do; PHP and C++ retry a non-empty match at the same position (`-a-----`) (PHP-C20, CPP-C26).
--- source
RREPLACE('b*?', "-", "abb")
--- expect
text "-a-b-b-"
===

### name: re.replace.alternation-empty-first
--- note
SPEC 7.8 (RREPLACE walks the matches left to right).
--- source
RREPLACE('(?:|a)', "-", "aa")
--- expect
text "-a-a-"
===

### name: re.replace.lazy-star-on-aab
--- note
SPEC 7.8 (RREPLACE walks the matches left to right).
--- source
RREPLACE('a*?', "-", "aab")
--- expect
text "-a-a-b-"
===

### name: re.replace.optional-lazy
--- note
SPEC 7.8 (RREPLACE walks the matches left to right).
--- source
COUNT(SPLIT(RREPLACE('x??', "-", "xx"), "-"))
--- expect
num 4
===

### name: re.limits.group-depth-at-the-cap
--- note
SPEC 7.8: group nesting is capped at MAX_DEPTH (200) in the shared validator, so acceptance does not depend on PCRE (refuses 251), SRELL (257) or Python's recursion (JS-C19, PY-C15, PHP-C45, CPP-C50).
--- source
RMATCH(REPEAT('(?:', 200) & 'a' & REPEAT(')', 200), "a")
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.limits.group-depth-past-the-cap
--- note

--- source
RMATCH(REPEAT('(?:', 201) & 'a' & REPEAT(')', 201), "a")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.limits.capturing-group-depth-at-the-cap
--- note
Capturing and non-capturing groups share the one depth.
--- source
RMATCH(REPEAT('(', 200) & 'a' & REPEAT(')', 200), "a")
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.limits.capturing-group-depth-past-the-cap
--- note

--- source
RMATCH(REPEAT('(', 201) & 'a' & REPEAT(')', 201), "a")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.limits.group-depth-far-past-the-cap
--- note
A 50,000-deep pattern recursed Python and Lisp to a host crash; it is `E_REGEX_SYNTAX` at the cap like any other.
--- source
RMATCH(REPEAT('(?:', 50000) & 'a' & REPEAT(')', 50000), "a")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.limits.group-depth-checked-at-compile-time
--- note
A literal pattern past the cap is caught at compile time, in a branch that never runs.
--- source
IF(FALSE, RMATCH('(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:(?:a)))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))', "a"), 1)
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.limits.group-count-at-the-cap
--- note
SPEC 7.8: at most MAX_REGEX_GROUPS (1000) groups in a pattern. (CPP-C50: compile time was super-linear in the number of groups, and RE2 refuses large programs.)
--- source
RMATCH('^' & REPEAT('(a)', 1000) & '$', REPEAT("a", 1000))
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.limits.group-count-past-the-cap
--- note

--- source
RMATCH('^' & REPEAT('(a)', 1001) & '$', REPEAT("a", 1001))
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.limits.non-capturing-groups-count
--- note
Non-capturing groups count toward the same cap.
--- source
RMATCH('^' & REPEAT('(?:a)', 1001) & '$', REPEAT("a", 1001))
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.limits.sequential-groups-do-not-nest
--- note
1000 groups in a row nest one deep: the depth cap and the count cap are separate rules.
--- source
RMATCH('^' & REPEAT('(?:a)', 1000) & '$', REPEAT("a", 1000))
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.limits.pattern-length-at-the-cap
--- note
SPEC 7.8: at most MAX_REGEX_PATTERN (65 535) code points in a pattern.
--- source
RMATCH('^' & REPEAT('a', 65533) & '$', REPEAT("a", 65533))
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.limits.pattern-length-past-the-cap
--- note

--- source
RMATCH('^' & REPEAT('a', 65535) & '$', REPEAT("a", 65535))
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.limits.pattern-length-counts-code-points
--- note
The cap is in code points, not bytes or UTF-16 units: 32,000 two-byte letters are far under it.
--- source
RMATCH('^' & REPEAT('ż', 32000) & '$', REPEAT("ż", 32000))
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.limits.repeat-product-is-not-a-program-size
--- note
`a{n}` bounds are capped individually at 65 535 and a pattern's length at 65 535 code points; the product of nested counts is not a limit the language states. It must not be a host failure: it is a value or ... FALSE here, because the subject is one `a`.
--- source
RMATCH('(?:a{60000}){60000}', "a")
--- expect
bool FALSE
===

### name: re.reject.collating-element-anywhere
--- note
SPEC 7.8: POSIX bracket forms include `[.x.]` (JS-C18, PHP-C19).
--- source
RMATCH('[a[.x.]]', "a")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.collating-element-first
--- note

--- source
RMATCH('[[.x.]]', "x")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.equivalence-class-anywhere
--- note
`[=x=]`, same rule.
--- source
RMATCH('[a[=x=]]', "a")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.reject.equivalence-class-first
--- note

--- source
RMATCH('[[=x=]]', "x")
--- expect
error E_REGEX_SYNTAX
===

### name: re.accept.bracket-then-dot-in-class
--- note
CONTROL: `[` and `.` in a class that do not form a POSIX bracket are literals.
--- source
RMATCH('^[[.]$', ".") AND RMATCH('^[[=]$', "=") AND RMATCH('^[.[]$', "[")
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.accept.nested-loop-with-a-nonnullable-body
--- note
CONTROL for the nullable-body rule: nesting loops is fine when every body must consume.
--- source
RMATCH('^(?:a+b)+$', "aabab")
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

### name: re.accept.optional-group-outside-a-loop
--- note
CONTROL: an optional group that is not inside a quantified group keeps its ordinary meaning in every engine.
--- source
RGROUPS('^(a)?b$', "b")
--- expect
tree -{"1"=t"b", "2"=t""}
===

### name: re.accept.empty-alternative-outside-a-loop
--- note
CONTROL: an empty alternative is fine when the group is not quantified.
--- source
RMATCH('^(?:a|)b$', "b")
--- expect
bool TRUE
===

